      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Few regrets voiced in Holborn and St Pancras over decision despite former PM having had ‘rough time of it’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/01/andy-burnham-statement-commons-prison-release-farage-healey-defence-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>In Keir Starmer’s north London constituency, full of pretty pubs and elegant townhouses, few tears were being shed at the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/01/keir-starmer-to-stand-down-as-mp\">news of his departure as its MP</a>.</p><p>One man nursing a pint outside a pub in Kentish Town simply remarked “good” when informed his MP had quit. He added: “I thought he was very nice before he became prime minister; I met him a few times. But he messed the country up and screwed over pensioners.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/01/keir-starmer-stepping-down-mp-constituents-holborn-st-pancras-kentish-town\">Continue reading...</a>"
